// FIELD SERVICE — REWIRED — one song: what it plays, how it is arranged, how it sounds.
//
// FIELD SERVICE as electro-disco, wired as a story — Claude's answer to GPT's LIVE WIRE
// (field-service-live-wire): the same tempo and the same parts, with a power cut, two
// drops that land, and the intro built to plumber-1's pixel-to-paper picture. A game
// alternate of plumber, selectable from the dev menu (GAME ALTERNATES) and on the desk.
// 
//   1–4    INSERT COIN — the hook on two pulse channels (tune, and plumber's own third
//          under it), triangle bass, noise drums, the whole mix crushed; the power dies
//          on 4.4 (every lane cut, a pew falling) — plumber-1's power-down sixteenth.
//          The cabinet screen loops 1–2.
//   5–8    REWIRING — paper lands on 5.1, the robot says FIELD SERVICE; motor and copper
//          arp open from dark; the hook's head climbs F G Am E7; cut on 8.2, the robot
//          again into the drop.
//   9–24   LIVE WIRE — A A B B A A C C on the electric grand + loud plain square, octave
//          motor in the kick's gaps, pumping supersaws; from 17 ice bell 8va, plumber's
//          harmony on PWM, brass in the hook's gaps.
//   25–32  BLACKOUT — short circuit on 25.1; the C then A phrase at half speed on the
//          grand over a string machine (Fmaj7 Cmaj7 Dm9 G6 | Am9 Dm9 Fmaj9 Dm7); copper
//          creeps back, the kick returns as a heartbeat, the power flickers on 32.3.
//   33–36  POWER UP — G A Bm F#7 (the key turns on G); cut on 36.3, the robot: REWIRED.
//   37–52  FULL POWER — the drop in B minor: + mega saw on the hook, ride, copper 16ths,
//          a stutter roll into 45.
//   53–56  SIGN OFF — the A phrase half speed back in A minor (Fmaj7 Dm9 Esus4 E7); the
//          mix crushes back to 8-bit and powers down on 56.4. The loop is 5–56.
// 
// The melody is plumber's, pitch for pitch, wherever the hook plays. Spot FX (crush,
// cuts, short circuit, flicker, filter openings, stutter) live in the automation and are
// laid by the generator.
// 
